# BYTE — PHASE 4 MASTER PROMPT
# COMPLETE BACKEND, DATABASE, API AND DATA MANAGEMENT IMPLEMENTATION

You are now responsible for implementing the backend infrastructure of BYTE, an existing smart campus food-services platform.

BYTE already has an established frontend, visual identity, navigation, menu layouts, login interface, outlet pages and multiple user-facing screens.

The existing frontend is working reasonably well. The purpose of this phase is to transform BYTE from a primarily frontend-driven application into a genuinely functional, database-driven full-stack application.

This is a substantial engineering task.

Your highest priorities are:

1. Preserve the existing frontend.
2. Build a reliable backend.
3. Establish a properly structured relational database.
4. Connect every relevant frontend feature to real backend APIs.
5. Implement authentication and permissions.
6. Implement genuine CRUD operations.
7. Make orders and table reservations persist correctly.
8. Ensure that errors, missing data and failed API requests never crash the application.

Do not sacrifice reliability to implement features quickly.

