# PART D — DATABASE RELATIONSHIPS AND INTEGRITY

Implement the following rules.

1. One campus can have multiple outlets.
2. One outlet can have multiple categories.
3. One category can have multiple menu items.
4. One user can place multiple orders.
5. One order belongs to exactly one outlet.
6. One order contains one or more order items.
7. One vendor can manage their assigned outlets.
8. Outlet staff can access only authorised outlet operations.
9. Administrators can manage campus-wide operations.
10. Reservations must respect table or outlet capacity.
11. Stock cannot become negative.
12. Prices cannot be negative.
13. Invalid order state transitions must be rejected.

Use foreign keys, unique constraints, transactions and indexes.

Use database transactions for order creation, payment-state updates and reservations.

Use appropriate concurrency protection to prevent two users from reserving the same table or purchasing unavailable stock simultaneously.

