# PART I — CART AND ORDER MANAGEMENT

Implement a complete customer ordering workflow.

## I1. Cart rules

- Add menu items.
- Remove menu items.
- Change quantities.
- Calculate totals.
- Validate item availability.
- Validate stock.
- Persist cart appropriately.

CRITICAL BUSINESS RULE:

A cart can contain items from only one outlet.

If a customer adds an item from another outlet while their cart contains items, ask whether they want to clear the existing cart and switch outlets.

Do not silently combine different outlets.

## I2. Order creation

When the customer checks out:

1. Verify authentication.
2. Verify outlet availability.
3. Retrieve current menu prices from the database.
4. Verify item availability.
5. Verify stock.
6. Recalculate totals on the server.
7. Apply valid taxes or charges.
8. Create order and order items transactionally.
9. Create the sandbox payment record.
10. Generate a unique order number.
11. Generate a secure pickup token.
12. Return the confirmed order.

Never trust the frontend to calculate or determine the final order price.

Prevent duplicate orders using idempotency protection.

## I3. Order status lifecycle

Implement controlled transitions:

PLACED → ACCEPTED → PREPARING → READY → COMPLETED

Support appropriate cancellation and rejection states.

Record:

- Previous status.
- New status.
- Timestamp.
- User or staff member responsible.

Only authorised users may update order status.

## I4. Pickup verification

- Generate a unique pickup token.
- Display the token to the customer.
- Allow authorised outlet staff to verify it.
- Prevent reuse.
- Record successful verification.
- Complete the order only after valid pickup verification.

